    the normal-drift version) which is perhaps a little surprising result 
    (assuming that all assumptions that is made are reasonable).
 


  * Scenario 3
    As noted above a Stanine score of 9/9 actually means that the score is > 126,
    so let's adjust for that by making StartIQ (at age 19) a random variable
    with the conditional probability:

      normal(100,15) > 126

    min_accepted_samples = 10000
